# ── text-to-music generation (Stable Audio Open + MusicGen + Riffusion) ──
# diffusers ships StableAudioPipeline since 0.27. Pinned to 0.32.2 here
# because newer releases (0.38+) require a pre-release safetensors,
# which doesn't pass our hash-locked supply-chain gate. Stable Audio Open
# is CUDA-only (engines.json flags it) — ~12 GB VRAM at fp16, no vocals,
# 47-second cap. Best for loops / SFX / textures. Riffusion (also CUDA-only)
# uses diffusers' StableDiffusionPipeline. MusicGen ships in transformers
# (no extra dep). All four music-gen engines are CUDA-only in engines.json;
# the CPU image still carries diffusers so the engine code import-paths
# resolve, but no music-gen engine is registered in engines-cpu.json.
#
# torchsde is a transitive dep of Stable Audio Open's
# CosineDPMSolverMultistepScheduler — diffusers doesn't pull it in as a
# hard dep, so it has to be listed explicitly.
#
# ACE-Step + DiffRhythm were considered for the initial release:
#   - ACE-Step needs AceStepPipeline from diffusers >= 0.38, which itself
#     requires a pre-release safetensors — revisit when safetensors 0.8.x
#     ships stable, or vendor the pipeline directly.
#   - DiffRhythm is an unpackaged research repo (no setup.py / PyPI release).
#     Revisit on upstream packaging or thirdparty/ vendoring.
diffusers==0.32.2
torchsde==0.2.6
